 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the social services law, in relation to requiring local social\nservices districts to provide luggage to children in foster care",
    "basePrintNo": "S8791",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8791-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §398-f, Soc Serv L (as proposed in S.3781 & A.5434)",
    "lawSection": "Social Services Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8791\n\nSPONSOR: BRISPORT\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the social services law, in relation to requiring local\nsocial services districts to provide luggage to children in foster care\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis chapter amendment clarifies provisions of L.2025, C.684.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends the underlying chapter by removing detailed\ndefinitions, eligibility, and reporting requirements for foster chil-\ndren's luggage; adding a clear definition of \"luggage\"; shifting respon-\nsibility for supplying and replacing luggage to local social services;\nand making expenditures for luggage eligible for state reimbursement.\n\nSubdivision 1 amends the underlying chapter by removing definitions\nrelated to luggage for children in foster care and adding a definition\nof \"luggage\" as a durable, reusable container designed to hold personal\nbelongings, excluding disposable bags, trash bags, and cardboard boxes.\n\nSubdivision 2 amends the underlying chapter by removing previous eligi-\nbility criteria that specified which foster youth qualify to receive\nluggage. It shifts responsibility for providing luggage from the Office\nof Children and Family Services to local social services districts.\nLocal districts are authorized to replace lost, stolen, or damaged\nluggage at their discretion.\n\nSubdivision 3 amends the underlying chapter, clarifying that any luggage\nprovided under this section may not be reclaimed or retained by the\nOffice of Children and Family Services, local social services districts,\nvoluntary agencies, or foster parents.\n\nLastly, subdivision 4 amends the underlying chapter to specify that\neligible expenditures for luggage supplied under this section are\nsubject to state reimbursement under the foster care block grant, in\naccordance with applicable law. Previously required reporting require-\nments have been removed.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is a negotiated change to the underlying chapter.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 684 of the Laws of 2025.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as a\nchapter of the laws of 2025 amending the social services law relating to\nrequiring the office of children and family services to provide luggage\nto youth in foster care, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S.\n3781 and A. 5434, takes effect.\n",
